  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "Tvc43sQSpjlJtRanHv0HOIclp/g=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:25:54.901Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Glintt is recorded as an Iberian healthtech leader through Glintt Life, running its own healthtech products. The screen's judgement is that it is product-led, and that is the disqualifier \u2014 not the vertical, which is a good one, and not the platform, since there is no third-party platform to complement.\n\nThe product-led exclusion works the same way here as elsewhere in the workbook: a firm that ships its own software has an internal roadmap that any new record layer competes with, and a revenue model that does not depend on assembling other people's components. Partnering asks it to route feature demand outward instead of into its own backlog.\n\nOne caveat on the record itself: the figures held for Glintt are twelve years old, dating from 2014. Anything size- or growth-dependent in this assessment is therefore unreliable, and the only durable part of the verdict is the model \u2014 product-led \u2014 which is a structural property unlikely to have reversed.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**9 \u00b7 do not pitch**\n- Glintt (PT)\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> Glintt Life is an Iberian healthtech leader. Product-led. Figures 12 years old (2014).",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:25:54.901231Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:25:54.901235Z"
    }
  },
